id: pm-rust-owzm
title: Track pm-cli 2026.10.19 as the parity oracle
description: "Bump the tests/oracle pin from 2026.10.14 to 2026.10.19, keep native parity and full coverage green"
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: ci,conformance,oracle,toolchain
created_at: "2026-10-20T05:19:59.230Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T17:32:56.758Z"
deadline: "2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: pi-agent
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: tests/oracle package.json and lockfile pin @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.19; COMPATIBLE_PM_VERSION matches; just release-check green at unchanged thresholds; every parity delta classified
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-rust-4ld8,related,"2026-10-20T05:19:59.230Z",pi-agent,"cli:create:dep",detected
comments[28]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T05:19:59.230Z",pi-agent,"Created for the oracle-currency update: pin tests/oracle to @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.19, run the full gate, classify all parity deltas."
  "2026-10-20T05:21:45.866Z",pi-agent,"Oracle pin bump applied: tests/oracle manifest and lockfile now pin @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.19 (regenerated with npm; new integrity recorded; bundled deps gained semver and OpenTelemetry api pins), COMPATIBLE_PM_VERSION in src/lib.rs and README oracle references updated. Merge drivers installed for this worktree against the 2026.10.19 oracle; strict health passes. Next: full just release-check and parity-failure classification."
  "2026-10-20T06:28:03.033Z",pi-agent,"Full parity-failure classification against the 2026.10.19 oracle, all verified empirically against the published 10.14 and 10.19 packages: (a) intended upstream changes: GH-1457 in 10.15 (explicit --limit binds under --no-truncate; no-truncate disables only the implicit token ceiling and the 10k row guard), GH-1465 in 10.17 (foreign principal release under warn governance emits ownership_warning:assignee_conflict in the release envelope; forced and bypass releases stay silent, strict still refuses), GH-1464 in 10.17 (successful warn-mode close returns follow_up kind complete_close_evidence with suggested_command/suggested_command_args instead of failure-shaped recovery), GH-1478 in 10.17 (240 UTF-16-unit string compaction steps back one unit to preserve surrogate pairs in JSON and TOON; no lone-surrogate escapes; the retained malformed-override refusal stays), GH-1481 in 10.18 (explicit --sort keys appear once in brief rows and projection.fields; title excluded as already present), GH-1489 in 10.18 (all-status spellings and terminal-family status filters keep the brief default; explicit --full and raw SDK full reads stay full). No upstream bug from the parity list surfaced as a divergence; upstream issues 1507 and 1509-1514 remain byte-kept quirks with no native fixes smuggled in. Native defects: none found; every failure mapped to an upstream behaviour change. Fixes: release envelope warning in mutation.rs ownership path, close follow_up receipt, list projection model (all-status brief, sort key in brief, explicit producer limit under no-truncate), pair-preserving compact_strings; golden list fixture regenerated from the 10.19 oracle with new full and full-all labels; differential and unit tests updated to the new contracts."
  "2026-10-20T07:12:40.212Z",pi-agent,"Progress: all 21 cargo test binaries pass against the 2026.10.19 oracle (514 integration+unit tests, 0 failures, including the previously red claim_release, close, list, output_parity and pagination suites). clippy -D warnings, fmt and rustdoc -D missing-docs gates pass. First branch-coverage run found 8 uncovered regions from the now-dead CLI-level lone-surrogate handler and one defensive match arm: the pair-preserving cut (GH-1478) can no longer manufacture a lone surrogate through the read pipeline, so the native CLI handler for the ToonEncoding detail was removed (the error variant and codec refusal stay covered by direct unit tests with retained malformed overrides, mirroring the upstream contract) and the defensive brief-row arm got a unit test. Re-running the coverage gate."
  "2026-10-20T07:58:56.127Z",codex-agent,"Read all handover comments and reviewed the uncommitted oracle/parity work. Continuing as codex-agent. Will resolve unreachable coverage paths without exclusions or lower thresholds, record behavioural revert proof, run the unchanged release gate, and verify all three CI platforms before releasing the claim. Registry currently reports 2026.10.20; this task deliberately remains scoped to the requested 2026.10.19 oracle."
  "2026-10-20T08:03:38.308Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof completed for all six intended deltas: reverting changed list selection/page functions fails unbounded_list_matches_published_cli_and_golden on all-status SDK output; reverting brief_row behavior fails brief_sort_values_survive_sdk_projection; reverting no-truncate limit handling fails no_truncate_still_refuses_invalid_explicit_limits; reverting close_item fails closure_sdk_fields_and_evidence_modes; reverting ownership_item_with_options fails claim_release_sequences_match_published_bytes_and_envelopes; restoring unconditional 240-unit compaction fails lossless_views_keep_cuts_and_javascript_numbers. Every reverted run exited 101 with assertion failures, not compile errors. Source restored after each proof. Strengthened the Unicode regression to assert the preserved prefix. Removed unreachable CLI handler and redundant compaction validation; retained the lossless codec contract via a documented constructor and refusal tests. No exclusions or threshold changes."
  "2026-10-20T08:14:37.628Z",codex-agent,"Fmt, clippy -D warnings and rustdoc gates pass. The foreground nice-wrapped pm test run is executing just release-check with the pinned oracle; shared-host load is high and mutation differential subprocesses are still progressing. Starting hosted CI alongside the local aggregate, with validation explicitly pending. Strict summary health with required merge drivers passes with the three existing advisories tracked by pm-rust-vuwe. Full health separately reconfirms the two untouched legacy chain mismatches on pm-rust-bj7a and pm-rust-unih already tracked by pm-rust-b4yl; no history repair or re-anchor is authorized or performed."
  "2026-10-20T08:31:07.819Z",codex-agent,"Hosted head 80099d6 passes the full Rust test jobs on Linux and macOS; Linux logs confirm 519 passing tests across all 21 binaries, with zero failed or ignored tests. All three native latency jobs and CodeQL/Rust analysis pass. Windows Rust tests and all three release aggregates remain pending. Clean-HOME execution with global/system Git configuration disabled also passes branch_merge_contract (1 test) and identity_audit (7 tests). Local nice-wrapped release-check is still progressing through the complete suite under shared-host load."
  "2026-10-20T08:34:16.958Z",codex-agent,"All three hosted Rust test jobs now pass on head 80099d6. Linux release coverage found one remaining reachable validation path: page_envelope propagates an invalid explicit limit under no-truncate when an offset bypasses first-page producer validation. Branches and functions were already 100%; one line and two aggregate regions remained uncovered. Extended the existing plain-tracker invalid-limit test with offset 0 to exercise this parser path, retaining the validation and all thresholds. Running targeted branch instrumentation before the next CI head."
  "2026-10-20T08:40:44.375Z",codex-agent,"Targeted nightly branch instrumentation passed no_truncate_still_refuses_invalid_explicit_limits with both first-page and offset-0 cases. The report confirms the previously uncovered page_envelope return region now executes (count 1). Exact command: cargo +nightly-2026-08-06 llvm-cov --locked --branch --lib --json --output-path OFFSET_COVERAGE_REPORT -- no_truncate_still_refuses_invalid_explicit_limits (run under nice -n 15; report retained locally). Hosted ordinary tests at 80099d6 passed across 21 binaries per OS: Linux 519, macOS 515, Windows 510; zero failures or ignored tests. The next push will include this test correction and the final local aggregate receipt."
  "2026-10-20T08:55:41.795Z",codex-agent,"Restarted the aggregate directly to preserve the requested actual nice level 15 and reproduce clean CI identity. The pm-linked runner had inherited extra niceness (19), so its identified gate process group was stopped after reaching pagination; no source was discarded. The environment already assigns nice 15, therefore nice -n 0 just release-check preserves that actual level. Fresh run uses a disposable HOME, disabled global/system Git configuration, and existing Rust toolchain caches. Fmt, clippy -D warnings and rustdoc pass again; both complete test passes will include the corrected offset case. All first-head OS coverage failures were the same page_envelope validation region, with no OS-specific defect."
  "2026-10-20T09:09:18.347Z",codex-agent,Created deferred follow-up pm-rust-qhem for the published 2026.10.20 oracle after complete local and GitHub duplicate searches. It remains open and unassigned; this delivery and PR 100 stay pinned to 2026.10.19. Existing tracker history/advisory work continues in pm-rust-b4yl and pm-rust-vuwe; those items were read and left unchanged.
  "2026-10-20T09:26:34.461Z",codex-agent,"Fresh clean-HOME foreground aggregate at actual nice 15 completed the ordinary pass: all 21 binaries and 519 tests pass with zero failed or ignored tests, including the corrected offset case. The branch-instrumented full pass is running now. Fmt, denied-warning clippy and private-item rustdoc gates passed in the same run. No coverage threshold or exclusion changed."
  "2026-10-20T09:41:00.456Z",codex-agent,"The complete clean-HOME run passed all 519 ordinary and 519 instrumented tests, but coverage still showed two missing production-library regions despite the unit-test build covering their source spans. The unit-only offset case alone was insufficient for aggregate coverage. Removed the genuinely unreachable unknown-sort-only arm by using the normal deadline metadata fallback for the remaining validated sort key, and consolidated explicit-limit parsing into one shared path for both truncation modes. This preserves all valid sort and limit behavior while removing redundant branches. No thresholds or exclusions changed; rerunning the full unchanged aggregate after focused verification."
  "2026-10-20T09:43:54.477Z",codex-agent,Focused verification of the final list cleanup passes all 14 list unit tests and denied-warning clippy. Expanded the existing row-guard test to prove no-truncate returns all 10000 rows without a producer limit but still returns 2 rows for an explicit limit. Expanded the existing optional sort metadata test for absent/present deadlines. Reverting only page_envelope to its pre-update implementation makes page_limits_offsets_and_deleted_item_fallback fail its assertion; final source restored. Full aggregate verification follows with both production and unit-test builds.
  "2026-10-20T11:05:19.845Z",codex-agent,"Final foreground clean-HOME just release-check at actual nice 15 is green. Ordinary and branch-instrumented passes each executed all 21 binaries: 519 passed and zero failed/ignored tests (1038 total executions). Coverage is exactly 100 percent: 13182 lines, 1365 functions, 22017 regions and 3154 branches, all covered. Fmt, denied-warning clippy, private-item rustdoc, audit and changelog check pass. Existing audit maintenance warning RUSTSEC-2024-0449 remains tracked separately. The pm-linked list::tests command passes all 14 tests. Production coverage was resolved by removing dead CLI/codec/unknown-sort-only paths and sharing explicit-limit parsing; retained lossless codec and deadline/limit behavior remain tested. Six parity-delta behavioural revert groups plus the refined single-function row-limit revert fail assertions as required. PR 100 links the full classification and pending final-head hosted checks. Dependabot 97 and 99 have plain supersession comments and are both closed; 97 was already closed. Implementation is frozen for hosted verification; item closure remains with the orchestrator."
  "2026-10-20T12:09:06.182Z",codex-agent,"PR #100 review round: fetched all review threads and their complete comment sets. One unresolved finding PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uUSXA is valid: the successful warn-close regression only checks follow_up.is_object(). Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Remote head is current and includes main. Plan: assert exact completion guidance on the non-git SDK fixture, inspect the whole PR for equivalent weak assertions, prove behavioral reverts fail, then run unchanged release and CI-equivalent gates. Threads will remain untouched."
  "2026-10-20T12:11:03.588Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uUSXA fixed in tests/support/mutation_unit.rs: assert exact follow_up kind, all missing flags, rendered command and full argument tokens; require closed status and no recovery. Complete-evidence off/warn/strict fixtures require no guidance. Whole-PR self-review found no equivalent weak receipt assertion; close differential tests already compare full envelopes. Behavioral revert proof: cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --lib closure_sdk_fields_and_evidence_modes fails assertions for six isolated production-only mutations (empty object, wrong kind, empty missing flags, empty args, wrong command, and old close_item recovery routing). All six compiled before failing; production source restored and focused test passes 1/1, zero ignored. The fixture is a real non-git tracker. No production change or threshold reduction is needed."
  "2026-10-20T12:53:58.456Z",codex-agent,"Review-round aggregate progress: clean-HOME just release-check has passed fmt, denied-warning clippy, private-item rustdoc and 437 completed ordinary tests across 16 binaries, with zero failed or ignored tests. All ownership (27), close (6), orientation (30), identity and list differential cases passed. Output parity and remaining suites are running; branch-instrumented full-suite verification follows. CI-equivalent strict summary health passes with the three existing advisories, and the locked release binary build passed. Focused linked test and six isolated behavioral negative proofs are already recorded above."
  "2026-10-20T12:55:10.607Z",codex-agent,"Progress count correction: the 437-test milestone above covered 15 completed binaries, not 16. Output parity and ownership contract subsequently passed as well, bringing the ordinary total to 443 tests across 17 completed binaries; pagination is running. All completed tests have zero failures and zero ignored cases."
  "2026-10-20T13:22:31.918Z",codex-agent,"Review-round ordinary full-suite pass is complete: all 21 binaries, 519 passed, zero failed and zero ignored tests under clean HOME with global/system Git configuration disabled. Fmt, denied-warning clippy and private-item rustdoc passed. The unchanged just release-check aggregate is now compiling and running its complete branch-instrumented pass; coverage remains required at 100 percent for lines, functions, regions and branches. No runtime changes were made during verification."
  "2026-10-20T14:08:49.394Z",codex-agent,"PR #100 review-round verification complete. Clean-HOME foreground just release-check passed at unchanged thresholds: ordinary and branch-instrumented passes each ran all 21 binaries, 519 passed and zero failed/ignored tests (1038 executions). Coverage is 100 percent: 13182/13182 lines, 1365/1365 functions, 22017/22017 regions and 3154/3154 branches. Fmt, denied-warning clippy, private-item rustdoc, audit and changelog check passed; audit retains the existing RUSTSEC-2024-0449 maintenance warning. CI-equivalent cargo +1.90.0 build --release --locked passed; cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --lib workspace::tests::single_item_get passed 2/2. node scripts/latency-gate.mts passed all 3 original 3000-item limits: get p95 10.02 ms below 50, list 96.85 below 150, context 216.90 below 250. The pm-linked receipt regression passed 1/1. Strict CI summary health passed all 8 checks with 3 pre-existing advisories. Six isolated production-only receipt mutations and old routing reversion are recorded above with assertion failures and restored source. Refreshed review data still has only PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uUSXA; latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Whole-PR self-review completed. Only assertions, evidence documentation and this item history change in this round. No new pm CLI or SDK bug encountered. Leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification; do not reply to or resolve the review thread."
  "2026-10-20T15:41:16.421Z",codex-agent,"PR 100 review round: fetched every unresolved thread and all comments (pagination exhausted). One unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uY9EN reports missing parent/deadline sort keys in intent brief rows. Latest CodeRabbit body has no Outside diff range findings. Branch is current with remote and contains origin/main. Verify against pinned oracle, add non-git regression and behavioral revert proof, inspect the complete PR diff for equivalent projection defects, then run the unchanged just release-check gate."
  "2026-10-20T15:46:34.239Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uY9EN verified valid against the pinned 2026.10.19 oracle. project_brief_rows now explicitly inserts null for an absent selected sort field, matching brief_row. Added real non-git SDK regression across every supported sort key and alias in both orders, with populated and absent parent/deadline values; CLI regression compares complete JSON and TOON wire output for both nullable sorts and orders. Linked pm test --run --match nullable_ --progress passed both commands (1 test each). Behavioral revert proof with tests retained: reverting only project_brief_rows compiled successfully and failed the SDK equality assertion on parent asc; the CLI regression compiled and failed its native/oracle byte comparison at the omitted parent:null field (both exit 101). Fixed source restored. The complete PR diff was reviewed for equivalent projection, sort-value, receipt and compaction defects; no other valid instance found. Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Starting unchanged clean-HOME just release-check."
  "2026-10-20T16:04:09.579Z",codex-agent,"Release-gate progress: fmt, denied-warning clippy and private-item rustdoc passed. The ordinary pass has completed 301 tests across three binaries with zero failed or ignored tests; 20 of 27 ownership differential cases have additionally passed while the rest continue under shared-host load. Clean-environment strict summary health passes all eight checks; the ordinary environment separately exposes a global extension-host version mismatch absent from the clean environment. Touched-item strict history verification passes all 63 current entries, and the 58 records inherited from the prior head remain byte-for-byte unchanged. No source changes during gate execution."
  "2026-10-20T16:22:43.148Z",codex-agent,"Ordinary release-gate progress: 408 tests passed across 14 completed binaries, zero failed or ignored tests. All 27 ownership differential cases, all 6 close differential cases, CLI dispatch, conformance, list and mutation checks passed. Orientation, output and remaining suites are running. Full branch-instrumented verification remains required afterward; no threshold or source changes have been made."
  "2026-10-20T17:23:12.065Z",codex-agent,"Ordinary release-gate progress: 504 tests passed across 20 completed binaries, zero failed or ignored tests. All 26 pagination cases passed, including the new nullable-intent JSON/TOON regression. The final 17-case search/collection differential suite is running. The loaded host makes this foreground gate slow; there have been no test timeouts. Actual scheduling priority is nice 19. The unchanged full branch-coverage pass and final audit/changelog checks remain required."
  "2026-10-20T17:32:56.757Z",codex-agent,The loaded host is still progressing through the final ordinary search/collection suite with no failures. Publishing the reviewed implementation and current evidence so hosted CI can run the identical unchanged just release-check aggregate in parallel with the foreground local gate. Current full-gate validation is explicitly pending; focused regressions and behavioral revert proofs are already complete. Keep this item in progress and claimed until final verification results are recorded.
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T05:19:59.230Z",pi-agent,"Oracle currency: pm-rust must track the current published pm CLI; this item owns the 2026.10.19 pin update"
